    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d35">

                <pb facs="0097" n="75" sameAs="frus:frus1950v05/pg75"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">886A.2553/8–3150: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to the Embassy in London
                        </hi><anchor n="1" xml:id="d35-f1"/>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">secret</hi>
                    </seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1950-08-31T19:00:00-04:00">August 31, 1950—7
                            p. m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>1157. For urinfo, SAG demanding complete renegotiation of 1933 Aramco concession
                    contract. Aramco Board has authorized Pres Moore to discuss renegotiation with
                    SAG. Revision contemplated by SAG cld be expected to have obvious repercussions
                    on other contracts in area, particularly since key issue appears to be Saudi
                    Arab demand for <pb facs="0098" n="76" xml:id="pg76"/> income tax for which co.
                    might obtain US Treas tax credit. No NE concessionnaire now pays local income
                    taxes.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">Acheson</hi>
                    </signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d35-f1" n="1" type="source" xml:id="d35-f1-content">
                <p>Repeated to Tehran as 391, Baghdad as 88, Jidda as 80, Moscow as 168, and Cairo
                    as 174.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
